[00:26.01]1. Mankind has stumbled for centuries in darkness.
[00:32.01]Vain is their quest as they try to catch the wind.
[00:38.20]Man’s tragic flaw is revealed in its starkness;
[00:44.20]None can they save, for they all have sinned.
[00:50.20](Chorus)
[00:56.20]Sing with good cheer, for God’s Kingdom is here!
[01:00.28]His Son’s mighty reign brings us freedom from fear.
[01:08.80]Through him, at last, evil soon will be past;
[01:15.54]This hope, like an anchor, is holding us fast.
[01:45.79]2. “God’s day is near!” rings the Kingdom proclamation;
[01:51.79]Men will no longer cry out to God: “How long?”
[01:57.79]Soon he will free all his groaning creation.
[02:03.72]Praise God Almighty, and join our song.
[02:19.10](Chorus)
[02:25.10]Sing with good cheer, for God’s Kingdom is here!
[02:31.10]His Son’s mighty reign brings us freedom from fear.
[02:38.60]Through him, at last, evil soon will be past;
[03:30.76]This hope, like an anchor, is holding us fast.